WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.910
"This story is fiction.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.910
All names of characters, places and

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.910
organizations in the story are fictional.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.910
Follow the traffic rules and drive safely."

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.120
No oncoming traffic.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.160
You can go all out!

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:45.290
All right! You're doing great, Mako!

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:47.270
Yeah...

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:48.690
What's the matter?

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:50.290
Is something on your mind?

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.420
Mako?

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:53.800
It's nothing.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.280
Okay, we're going for another run, Sayuki.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.060
Ah, the weather's awesome.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.910
Yeah, seriously.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:42.800
It makes me feel like driving somewhere instead of working.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:47.660
And if we could have a cute girl in our passenger seats...

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.160
Woah!

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.120
Why are you acting surprised?

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.310
How long were you standing there, Kenji-senpai?

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:53.500
What? Am I not supposed to be here?

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.610
Well, it's not a problem or anything.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.620
You must be bored.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:02.480
It's Takumi.

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:07.170
Yo.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:08.150
Hello.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:11.350
D doesn't have a race this week, right?

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.560
Yeah.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.340
So you're bored too?

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:19.090
Well, it's not like I'm bored, but...

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.390
I don't have work today or anything, so...

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.360
No problem, no problem.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.830
You came here 'cause you have nowhere better to go, right?

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.040
Bullseye.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.960
So how's your job at the shipping company?

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:34.790
Have you gotten used to it?

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:38.980
Yeah, but I've been busy because I'm involved with D.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.980
Hey, tell us about your battle the other day!

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:46.090
What're your feelings about your first victory as a member of Project D?

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.380
Well... um...

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:49.830
how should I put it?

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.650
It was a relief.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:52.520
A relief?

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.970
What, that's it?

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:58.360
You're not gonna say something like, 
"I knew victory was mine at that point"?

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.180
I mean,

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:04.240
I just drove like Ryosuke-san told me to.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.880
But I was happy that I won,

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:10.210
even though it was a close battle.

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.240
They praised me and said I did well.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:18.250
Racing outside the prefecture must be a lot of pressure.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:23.670
It'd be embarrassing if you challenged someone, traveled to their site, and lost.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:27.760
But I don't even think about things like that when I'm racing.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.970
Instead of things like wanting to win or how I can't afford to lose,

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:35.400
I think more about driving better than I did the last time.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.110
I see.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:39.690
I haven't even driven on the mountain pass,

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:42.300
much less been in a battle recently...

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:51.240
Say, Takumi, could you lend me some time tonight if you're not busy?

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.000
Sure.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.950
I don't have anything going on.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.650
I'm gonna try pushing myself on the mountain pass.

00:05:57.650 --> 00:05:59.690
I want you to sit next to me and teach me.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:00.460
All right?

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.190
That's a great idea!

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:05.550
Let's all get together on Akina again and have a blast!

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:06.970
Sure!

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:06.970
Yeah.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:25.440
I understand.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:28.340
It really makes me happy.

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:29.450
But...

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:34.810
please let me think about it for a little bit.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:37.770
It's been awhile since the four of us came up here.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:43.270
Yeah, I've only been driving on Akina for deliveries these days.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:48.280
It must be nerve-wracking to drive on a new course for your battles.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:49.980
Of course.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:54.260
Here at Akina, we know about the minute details of the course,

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:58.490
but things are completely different when it's your first time on a new course.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:02.250
Even though it's unavoidable as a member of Project D, it's gotta be scary.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.470
Yeah.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:12.770
Hey, let's get started soon, Iketani-senpai!

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:16.600
Kenji-senpai and I will stick right behind you in my 85.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:20.180
If you're too slow, I'm gonna pass you.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.910
Now you've said it.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.790
All right, Takumi, please get in.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:26.270
Sure.

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:32.760
I'm counting on you.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:35.920
If something comes to mind, please let me know, no matter how small the detail.

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.280
I understand.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:44.330
Well then, let's see what kind of driving he'll show us.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.160
This is exciting.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:47.420
Here I go!

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.380
He's started!

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:52.470
Don't get left behind.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:53.670
I know.

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:54.470
Go!

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.640
It's the first corner.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.480
A-all right...

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.400
Not bad!

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.660
H-how was that just now, Takumi?

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:26.370
Both your line selection and timing weren't too bad.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:27.860
Oh yeah?

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:35.260
His acceleration out of the corner is pretty good!

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.280
That's surprising.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:40.640
All right,

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.390
this feels good!

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:55.780
He's good.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:57.860
Not bad, Iketani!

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:04.580
How's that?

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.910
I'm in a groove today.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:10.080
The upcoming S-curve is gonna be a problem though.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:15.090
Iketani-senpai tends to push it too far when he gets cocky.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:19.160
Next up is the S-curve!

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:19.930
Yeah!

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:22.740
Here goes,

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:23.430
the S-curve!

00:10:26.570 --> 00:10:27.770
Iketani-senpai,

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:31.900
you're pushing it too much!

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:42.740
O-oh my God!

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.070
Oh man,

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:51.880
he's done it.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:53.700
Well, we knew this would happen.

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:09.480
Thank God, no scratches anywhere.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:13.230
You should at least change your right rear tire though.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:14.840
You're right.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.340
I'll change it when I get back.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.530
Man, I still need a lot of practice.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:23.780
But I guess I couldn't get as good as Takumi, even if I did practice.

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:26.680
It's just like you to be so wishy-washy.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.910
W-what's that supposed to mean?

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.500
And you know,

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:33.800
it's about time you got over that other thing too.

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:36.420
What's this all of a sudden?

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.630
What am I supposed to get over?

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:41.560
I'll take this opportunity to be blunt.

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:44.850
Forget about Mako-chan.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.100
M-Mako-chan? What about her?

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:51.360
At this rate, you're gonna be single for the rest of your life.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:53.530
You might lose out when a new opportunity comes your way,

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:57.110
because you're still dragging on about Mako-chan.

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:00.340
Hmm, that's very possible.

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:02.550
Don't exaggerate things like that.

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:03.820
That's bad luck.

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:05.960
I'm not exaggerating.

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:08.830
Watching you seriously worries me.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.220
It's none of your business.

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:14.730
First of all, I don't wanna hear it from another single man.

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:16.750
N-no! Iketani-senpai.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:19.710
It'll be the end once you say that to Kenji-senpai!

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:22.460
I...

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:25.000
I want a girlfriend too!

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:27.600
But you see...

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:29.420
You can't help what you don't have!

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:34.300
Are you two supposed to be a pair of comedians?

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:35.610
You might have a point.

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:44.240
Either way, you...

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.550
What is it?

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:48.860
Isn't your mind still filled with Mako-chan?

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:51.240
Why don't you try contacting her again?

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:54.120
That's impossible. Out of the question.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:57.370
I wouldn't be in a bind if I could do that.

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:01.050
I've tried many times. I just wuss out at the last second.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.960
Once you miss your chance,

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:04.420
it's over.

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:06.970
No kidding.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:11.310
I've lost track of how many times I wanted to call Kazumi-chan.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:15.920
You gradually lose your opportunities to make a move as time goes by...

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:19.520
It's already been half a year since then.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.480
What's the problem with half a year?

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:24.830
It's too late.

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:28.200
There's no way a cute girl like that would stay single for long.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.830
You don't know that.

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:34.330
Mako-chan isn't the same as those typical light-hearted girls.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:37.210
She wouldn't like it if I called her!

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:42.380
Anyway, it's too late.

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:45.510
I'm convinced of that much.

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:51.850
He's really holding it back.

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:56.460
I guess he needs some fated encounter to break him out.

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:13.580
A day hasn't gone by when I haven't thought of Mako-chan.

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:20.400
I've always thought that I need to apologize about that day.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:27.780
But you know what, Moon? That's what's so hard about this...

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:29.490
Huh?

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:32.970
Hey, a shooting star!

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:48.150
Man, a memorial service? What a drag.

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:52.360
It's kinda busy.

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:54.430
Is it because it's a holiday?

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:56.180
Say, Koichirou.

00:14:56.180 --> 00:14:56.910
Huh?

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:58.790
Is there a rest area coming up?

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:00.030
What?

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:01.720
Can't be helped I guess...

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:10.290
Hurry up, Mom!

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:12.010
We don't have a lot of time.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:14.140
Yeah, yeah, I know.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:15.270
Sheesh.

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:21.660
The rest of the world is on vacation, huh.

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:26.780
There are couples everywhere I look!

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:28.780
So where do you wanna go after that?

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:31.630
Well, anywhere's fine!

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:35.240
I want to go on a drive with a girl like that too.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:39.790
To think that the person sitting in the passenger's seat for my roadtrip is my mom...

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:45.020
It's depressing to the megaton-level.

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:49.060
What is it, Mom?

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.930
Stare...

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:56.690
Just as I thought! It's Iketani!

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:58.430
S-Sayuki-chan!

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:02.320
I thought it was someone else because you were dressed like that.

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:05.190
Hey Mako! It was Iketani after all!

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:07.690
What are you doing? Come over here already!

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:10.030
Mako-chan?

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.010
Hello.

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:23.820
I-it's been awhile.

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:26.480
Hey, what are you getting flustered for?

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:28.570
You sure are a weird man.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:30.350
W-well...

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:32.840
But man, this brings back memories. How's everyone doing?

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.890
Y-yeah...

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.010
Takumi-kun's sure amazing!

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:42.390
I've been making sure to check Project D's home page.

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:47.230
Is this reality?

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:50.610
Is that really Mako-chan in front of me?

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:53.970
At 8pm...

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:59.820
I'll be waiting for you under the billboard...

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:02.640
that I first met you at.

00:17:04.030 --> 00:17:05.620
Would you like to meet there

00:17:06.390 --> 00:17:13.110
and spend the night together somewhere quiet, where we can be alone?

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.190
Mako-chan is...

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:19.990
Mako-chan is right in front of my eyes...

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:23.450
Hey now, Iketani,

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:25.500
have you been listening to me at all?

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:26.150
Huh?

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:28.650
What's the matter with you, spacing out like that?

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:31.120
Oh sorry, Sayuki-chan.

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:34.650
I just remembered that there was something I just had to tell Mako-chan.

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:35.990
Huh?!

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:41.070
I... need to apologize to you, Mako-chan.

00:17:41.070 --> 00:17:42.590
I'm really sorry

00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:45.460
for not making it to our meeting on time.

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:49.500
On that day, the highway was really backed up.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:52.160
No, it wasn't just that.

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:55.400
It's also because I left late.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:58.390
Either way, it was past 10

00:17:58.390 --> 00:18:00.220
by the time I got to our meeting spot.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:02.350
What? You can't be serious...

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:05.730
I waited there until 10pm exactly.

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:07.040
No!

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:08.750
You must be joking.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:12.670
Mako-chan, you waited two hours for someone like me?!

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:13.730
Yes.

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.990
So back then...

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:21.680
Could it be that I missed her...

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:23.860
by just a minute or two?!

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:29.540
I really must've been out of luck.

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.510
No,

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:34.900
if I hadn't hesitated back then and left sooner...

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:36.800
Koichirou, what are you doing?

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:38.730
Gah!

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:39.840
Mom?!

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:41.670
It's nothing at all!

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:44.580
Hey, we'll be late if we don't get going.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:46.430
Your aunts will nag us.

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:47.980
I know that!

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:52.250
I'll be right there, so you don't need to come over here. You're embarrassing me!

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.590
God dammit!

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:56.470
Why do things always go like this?

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:59.170
My head's starting to spin,

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:00.950
but I'm not gonna back down!

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:06.870
Mako-chan,

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:10.210
I have other things I want to tell you,

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:12.340
but I don't have time today.

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:13.910
Um...

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:15.630
so...

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:16.610
I...

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:18.090
Me too.

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:22.400
I have something I want to tell you too, Iketani-san.

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:26.790
Please give me a call when you get the time.

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:28.060
I'll be waiting.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:30.110
M-Mako-chan...

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:32.330
I got it! I'll be sure to contact you.

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:34.680
W-well then...

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:36.460
Yeah. See you again.

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:45.960
Hey, what's the matter, Koichirou?

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:47.800
Who's that girl?

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:54.230
Oh, Koichirou...

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:55.380
Hey...

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:59.550
I don't remember how I got back to the car.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:04.330
My mind was blown for the next 30 minutes.

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:21.970
I have no doubts about it.

00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:26.310
This was surely destiny.

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:37.880
What?!

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.040
You met Mako-chan?

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:42.030
Is that true, Iketani-senpai?

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:44.020
That's right.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:46.510
Really, really, really for real.

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:49.980
I can't believe such a coincidence could happen.

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:53.460
I ran right into her at a rest area on the highway.

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:54.770
I see...

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:58.230
I'm convinced for sure this time.

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:04.230
This is my "last chance" that's been given to me by my revered ancestors.

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:05.230
D'oh!

00:21:05.230 --> 00:21:07.360
Why is it your ancestors?

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:11.040
Iketani-senpai, I thought your word of choice was "God"?

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:15.250
Not this time, because I was on my way to a memorial service.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:18.250
This guy has a surprisingly religious side to him.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:24.270
I can tell that time is being rewound at an incredible pace inside me right now.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:28.260
It's as if I'm in a time machine!

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:29.660
Huh.

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:35.550
It's as if I can almost go back to under that Kamameshi restaurant billboard.

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:39.860
Thank you, revered ancestors.

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:43.360
I... will never repeat the same mistake!

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:44.500
That's right.

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:45.540
Good luck!

00:21:45.540 --> 00:21:46.470
Yeah!

00:21:46.470 --> 00:21:52.900
My difficulties of the past six months have drilled into me the importance of acting with courage.

00:21:52.900 --> 00:21:54.620
I'll score for sure this time.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:57.640
I'm going to make a move on Mako-chan!

00:21:59.770 --> 00:22:00.740
An aura!

00:22:00.740 --> 00:22:02.430
He's emitting an aura!!

00:22:06.360 --> 00:22:09.140
I'm not sure what's going on, but you're impressing me.

00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:11.600
You've sure grown.

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:15.430
I can't believe you're the same indecisive Iketani.

00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:17.170
Yeah, really.

00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:18.820
Things really worked out.

00:22:18.820 --> 00:22:20.150
I'm happy for you, Iketani.

00:22:20.150 --> 00:22:22.330
Good luck this time.

00:22:22.330 --> 00:22:24.090
I think you definitely have a shot.

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:26.400
Make sure you get your beloved Mako-chan!

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:30.490
Whoa.

00:22:30.490 --> 00:22:32.240
He sure seems confident.

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:47.770
Why?

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:50.470
Why am I hesitating at the last moment?

00:22:51.410 --> 00:22:54.150
I can't decide. What am I supposed to do?

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:02.250
Mako.

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:04.300
There's a car coming up.

00:23:05.130 --> 00:23:05.780
Okay.

00:23:09.820 --> 00:23:11.460
Did you see that?

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:13.140
They were women.

00:23:13.140 --> 00:23:14.390
Oh?

00:23:14.390 --> 00:23:16.040
Female racers, huh?

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:28.600
Not bad...

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:31.010
but you should be able to go faster.

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:32.190
Okay.

00:23:32.990 --> 00:23:34.470
I'll go for another run.

00:23:46.520 --> 00:23:48.280
Here they come, here they come.

00:23:57.910 --> 00:24:00.660
Hey, missies!

00:24:01.610 --> 00:24:03.220
Hey!

00:24:10.090 --> 00:24:12.640
You're looking pretty good.

00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:16.100
Say, won't you give us a tip or two?

00:24:21.100 --> 00:24:23.570
Hey now, you're gonna totally ignore us?

00:24:23.570 --> 00:24:25.960
Hah! Acting so stuck up...

00:24:25.960 --> 00:24:28.610
you two probably came up here looking for men.

00:24:28.610 --> 00:24:32.110
They must be full of themselves just because they can drive a little.

00:24:32.110 --> 00:24:35.240
Drive? They're just women in the end.

00:24:36.410 --> 00:24:38.120
So what if we're female?

00:24:38.120 --> 00:24:41.400
Oh, now she's heating up.

00:24:42.370 --> 00:24:47.250
Getting looked down on just for being female pisses us off like nothing else.

00:24:47.250 --> 00:24:49.000
How scary!

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:52.560
So, you wanna race us?

00:24:52.560 --> 00:24:54.720
A single downhill run.

00:24:55.270 --> 00:24:57.170
What do you think, Mako?

00:24:57.170 --> 00:25:00.470
If we don't accept, they'll say we ran away because we're women.

00:25:00.470 --> 00:25:02.860
That's the way! Let's do it.

00:25:02.860 --> 00:25:03.810
Yeah.

00:25:04.580 --> 00:25:08.060
We'll go with the leader-chaser format.
Leave the other in the dust or overtake to win.

00:25:08.060 --> 00:25:10.390
You guys can lead.

00:25:11.500 --> 00:25:12.830
All right.

00:25:12.830 --> 00:25:14.620
Let's have them cry like babies.

00:25:17.260 --> 00:25:19.150
Let's go then!

00:25:29.210 --> 00:25:32.800
Do those women really think that they can beat me?

00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:34.510
What should we do when we win?

00:25:34.510 --> 00:25:36.290
Maybe we can get some...

00:25:41.430 --> 00:25:42.460
Good,

00:25:42.460 --> 00:25:44.590
we'll let them run for a little bit.

00:25:45.280 --> 00:25:48.150
We'll take it to them at the exit of corner C-121 like usual.

00:25:48.150 --> 00:25:49.060
Okay.

00:26:05.620 --> 00:26:07.310
They're better than we thought.

00:26:07.310 --> 00:26:08.450
Yeah,

00:26:08.450 --> 00:26:09.330
but...

00:26:10.660 --> 00:26:12.340
they're not anyone I'd lose to.

00:26:15.330 --> 00:26:17.400
Hey, start trying a little.

00:26:17.400 --> 00:26:18.850
They're sticking right to us!

00:26:19.760 --> 00:26:21.600
This is impossible.

00:26:22.240 --> 00:26:23.830
What's going on?

00:26:29.010 --> 00:26:30.330
Amazing.

00:26:30.330 --> 00:26:32.110
You're amazing, Mako.

00:26:32.110 --> 00:26:36.110
You're definitely faster than when we raced against Takumi-kun.

00:26:39.090 --> 00:26:41.320
Your entry speed into corners,

00:26:41.320 --> 00:26:44.010
braking, choice of lines...

00:26:44.700 --> 00:26:46.500
they're all perfect.

00:26:58.560 --> 00:27:01.500
We don't need to wait until C-121.

00:27:01.960 --> 00:27:03.720
I'm passing him on the next corner!

00:27:11.560 --> 00:27:13.430
N-no way!

00:27:13.430 --> 00:27:14.230
Hey!

00:27:26.040 --> 00:27:27.580
Unbelievable!

00:27:36.980 --> 00:27:39.630
You've become independent, Mako...

00:28:48.720 --> 00:28:50.950
Well then, Kenji, Itsuki,

00:28:50.950 --> 00:28:52.500
I'll be on my way.

00:28:52.500 --> 00:28:53.200
What?

00:28:53.200 --> 00:28:54.560
Already?

00:28:54.560 --> 00:28:56.730
You sure are leaving early.

00:28:56.730 --> 00:28:59.130
Weren't you meeting her at night?

00:28:59.130 --> 00:29:01.970
I can't be careful enough.

00:29:01.970 --> 00:29:06.720
After all, it wouldn't be funny if I was late again today.

00:29:06.720 --> 00:29:09.850
Even so, don't you think you're going too soon?

00:29:09.850 --> 00:29:11.490
It's fine.

00:29:11.490 --> 00:29:15.500
Mako-chan waited two hours for me.

00:29:16.150 --> 00:29:20.980
If you think about that, getting there two hours early is nothing.

00:29:20.980 --> 00:29:23.530
Well, you have a point when you put it that way.

00:29:23.530 --> 00:29:25.400
Either way, I'm off.

00:29:25.400 --> 00:29:28.780
I can't fail if I'm a step ahead on every move.

00:29:29.630 --> 00:29:30.890
Good luck!

00:29:30.890 --> 00:29:32.680
Hurrah! Hurrah!

00:29:32.680 --> 00:29:34.560
Iketani-senpai!

00:29:41.700 --> 00:29:42.630
So he's gone?

00:29:42.630 --> 00:29:46.380
Iketani-senpai's unbelievably invested in this.

00:29:46.380 --> 00:29:47.550
Yeah,

00:29:47.550 --> 00:29:50.510
his last mistake must really have smarted.

00:29:50.510 --> 00:29:52.330
I wonder what'll happen...

00:29:52.330 --> 00:29:53.600
It makes me nervous.

00:29:53.600 --> 00:29:58.360
From what I've heard from Iketani, I think he's got a pretty good chance...

00:29:59.060 --> 00:30:03.610
It sounds like Mako-chan was waiting all this time for him to contact her too.

00:30:03.610 --> 00:30:06.420
In that case, I think something big's about to happen!

00:30:08.860 --> 00:30:12.730
Iketani had a serious crush on Mako-chan, after all...

00:30:12.730 --> 00:30:16.790
It'd be like a dream for him if a girl like that became his girlfriend.

00:30:16.790 --> 00:30:19.290
The thought of it makes me jealous.

00:30:19.290 --> 00:30:21.840
And what about you, Kenji-senpai?

00:30:21.840 --> 00:30:26.000
Well to be honest, I used to be really jealous too.

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:28.000
Mako-chan's pretty, after all.

00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:29.190
Yeah, really.

00:30:29.190 --> 00:30:31.180
That's to be expected of any man!

00:30:31.180 --> 00:30:32.520
But you know,

00:30:32.520 --> 00:30:36.060
I truly feel like cheering him on now.

00:30:36.060 --> 00:30:39.440
I get the feeling that I'll get an earful of bragging on a daily basis,

00:30:39.440 --> 00:30:41.230
but I'll take it for his sake.

00:30:42.710 --> 00:30:45.990
You're bringing tears to my eye! Now that's a manly friendship!

00:30:45.990 --> 00:30:49.200
I just can't turn my back on him.

00:30:49.200 --> 00:30:51.410
I worry more about him than about myself.

00:30:51.410 --> 00:30:53.110
That's true.

00:30:53.110 --> 00:30:56.880
I want Iketani-senpai to find happiness too.

00:30:56.880 --> 00:30:58.320
Hey now,

00:30:58.320 --> 00:31:01.150
stop cheering for Iketani...

00:31:01.150 --> 00:31:05.280
and go find a girlfriend or two for yourselves already.

00:31:05.960 --> 00:31:08.510
Youth is short.

00:31:08.510 --> 00:31:10.990
Please don't remind me...

00:31:12.290 --> 00:31:13.670
My heart is aching.

00:31:13.670 --> 00:31:15.500
Kazumi-chan...

00:31:17.370 --> 00:31:19.940
And I have no one...

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:32.930
I'm surprisingly calm.

00:31:34.390 --> 00:31:39.000
Even though I'm about to confess my feelings to a girl for the first time in my life...

00:31:42.530 --> 00:31:44.740
"Please date me."

00:31:44.740 --> 00:31:47.000
I just need to say that one sentence.

00:31:47.670 --> 00:31:49.470
I have no expectations.

00:31:49.470 --> 00:31:50.740
I'm just going to throw my everything at her.

00:31:51.920 --> 00:31:55.620
When I think about my half year of constant regret,

00:31:55.620 --> 00:31:57.970
I have no doubts holding me back!

00:32:10.900 --> 00:32:13.200
Oh boy...

00:32:13.200 --> 00:32:17.660
The highway was empty, so I really did get here two hours early.

00:32:17.660 --> 00:32:19.350
Oh well.

00:32:19.350 --> 00:32:22.460
Now I'll be 100% on time.

00:32:22.460 --> 00:32:24.870
When I think about the six months leading up to today,

00:32:24.870 --> 00:32:26.910
two hours is nothing.

00:32:54.620 --> 00:32:56.180
Excuse me...

00:32:56.180 --> 00:32:56.950
Huh?

00:32:56.950 --> 00:33:00.110
I saw that you've been sitting there

00:33:00.110 --> 00:33:03.850
and don't seem to be in a hurry.

00:33:03.850 --> 00:33:07.210
Do you think you could listen to what I have to say?

00:33:13.560 --> 00:33:15.050
What?!

00:33:15.050 --> 00:33:18.550
Your tour bus left while you were eating some kamameshi?!

00:33:18.550 --> 00:33:20.180
That's right.

00:33:20.180 --> 00:33:23.470
So I have a favor to ask of you.

00:33:23.470 --> 00:33:29.440
I'm very sorry for the trouble, but could you drive me to my hotel in Karuizawa?

00:33:29.440 --> 00:33:32.440
I'd really rather not...

00:33:32.440 --> 00:33:34.780
I know it's a lot of trouble,

00:33:34.780 --> 00:33:40.130
but I'm not familiar with this area and I don't know my left from my right.

00:33:40.130 --> 00:33:43.350
I was really starting to get lonely.

00:33:47.020 --> 00:33:48.470
Won't you?

00:33:49.990 --> 00:33:51.460
As I expected...

00:33:52.250 --> 00:33:54.240
Oh man...

00:33:54.240 --> 00:33:56.010
I'm starting to feel sorry for him.

00:33:56.010 --> 00:34:01.510
I could make it to Karuizawa and back in an hour.

00:34:03.970 --> 00:34:05.660
All right,

00:34:05.660 --> 00:34:07.600
I'll take you there, gramps.

00:34:07.600 --> 00:34:08.700
Huh?

00:34:08.700 --> 00:34:10.000
Really?

00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:11.870
Oh, thank you.

00:34:11.870 --> 00:34:16.250
Please, please, you're a good person!

00:34:16.250 --> 00:34:18.040
Okay, hurry and get in.

00:34:18.040 --> 00:34:18.860
Okay.

00:34:30.390 --> 00:34:33.250
Are you traveling by yourself, gramps?

00:34:33.250 --> 00:34:35.640
That's right.

00:34:35.640 --> 00:34:39.010
At my age, traveling is about the only fun in your life.

00:34:39.010 --> 00:34:40.720
I see...

00:34:40.720 --> 00:34:46.600
Spring, summer, fall, winter:

00:34:46.600 --> 00:34:51.310
they all have their own flavors.

00:34:51.730 --> 00:34:55.630
Now that he mentions it, it's spring already.

00:34:56.160 --> 00:34:59.130
The seasons sure go by quickly.

00:35:04.450 --> 00:35:08.540
Oh yeah, where in Karuizawa is your hotel, gramps?

00:35:08.540 --> 00:35:10.890
Well...

00:35:10.890 --> 00:35:14.040
I think I had a pamphlet.

00:35:21.120 --> 00:35:22.720
Oh, here it is.

00:35:22.720 --> 00:35:25.180
I'd like for you to take me here.

00:35:27.950 --> 00:35:30.820
What? Kitakaru Grand Hotel?

00:35:30.820 --> 00:35:32.930
Wait a minute, gramps,

00:35:32.930 --> 00:35:35.960
although it is Karuizawa, this is in North Karuizawa!

00:35:36.710 --> 00:35:37.780
It is Karuizawa, no?

00:35:37.780 --> 00:35:40.330
North Karuizawa is in Gunma Prefecture.

00:35:40.330 --> 00:35:43.100
It's far away! I can't do that.

00:35:47.700 --> 00:35:51.280
I can't say no to that face!

00:35:51.280 --> 00:35:54.200
Crap, what a nightmare.

00:35:54.200 --> 00:35:58.130
Two hours is barely enough for North Karuizawa...

00:35:58.920 --> 00:36:02.420
Please give me a call when you get the time.

00:36:02.420 --> 00:36:03.640
I'll be waiting.

00:36:03.640 --> 00:36:05.790
M-Mako-chan...

00:36:05.790 --> 00:36:07.890
I got it! I'll be sure to contact you.

00:36:07.890 --> 00:36:09.930
W-well then...

00:36:09.930 --> 00:36:11.050
Yeah.

00:36:11.050 --> 00:36:12.590
See you again.

00:36:13.720 --> 00:36:18.320
No, but if I give it my best, I'll be able to get back on time.

00:36:19.150 --> 00:36:21.170
Gramps, I'm gonna step on it.

00:36:21.170 --> 00:36:22.680
Please hang on!

00:36:59.900 --> 00:37:02.000
He's not here yet.

00:37:02.000 --> 00:37:05.510
I got here first again.

00:37:09.990 --> 00:37:12.380
I'm such an idiot!

00:37:13.830 --> 00:37:15.650
Half a year ago,

00:37:15.650 --> 00:37:17.560
I messed everything up by being two hours late.

00:37:18.260 --> 00:37:21.830
Today, I messed up by being two hours early.

00:37:21.830 --> 00:37:24.340
This is too much, revered ancestors!

00:37:35.230 --> 00:37:38.440
If only I was Takumi at a time like this...

00:37:44.990 --> 00:37:46.490
Shit!

00:37:49.030 --> 00:37:50.630
Either way, I need to hurry.

00:37:50.630 --> 00:37:53.600
If I speed, I should only be about 30 minutes late.

00:37:54.710 --> 00:37:58.710
I've trained my driving technique for a time like this!

00:39:01.000 --> 00:39:03.150
I... I've done it...

00:39:03.840 --> 00:39:06.650
I hit a rock on the shoulder of the road...

00:39:06.650 --> 00:39:07.870
and burst a tire.

00:39:07.870 --> 00:39:09.270
This is the worst!

00:39:13.220 --> 00:39:14.890
I don't have a spare!

00:39:25.840 --> 00:39:30.070
You should at least change your right rear tire though.

00:39:30.430 --> 00:39:31.790
That's right!

00:39:31.790 --> 00:39:33.300
I changed my tire back then and...

00:39:33.300 --> 00:39:34.810
Shit!

00:39:34.810 --> 00:39:36.830
And at a time like this!

00:39:37.630 --> 00:39:40.500
Oh yeah, I need to call her at least...

00:39:44.690 --> 00:39:47.680
Why is my battery out?!

00:39:48.780 --> 00:39:50.570
I can't waste time here!

00:39:53.700 --> 00:39:55.720
Mako-chan, I'm so sorry!

00:39:55.720 --> 00:40:00.310
Mako-chan!

00:40:11.210 --> 00:40:13.840
I wonder what happened to Iketani-san...?

00:40:13.840 --> 00:40:16.130
He's not even calling.

00:40:16.130 --> 00:40:17.300
I wonder...

00:40:17.300 --> 00:40:18.990
if he forgot?

00:40:28.930 --> 00:40:32.380
There's not even a public phone in the mountains like this.

00:40:36.240 --> 00:40:37.950
Ouch...

00:40:37.950 --> 00:40:39.430
shit.

00:40:39.430 --> 00:40:41.540
My heart's about to burst.

00:40:41.540 --> 00:40:43.930
I need to find a phone!

00:40:51.790 --> 00:40:55.840
A racer is racing down the mountain pass on his own feet...

00:40:55.840 --> 00:40:57.850
This isn't even funny!

00:41:15.390 --> 00:41:16.650
Hello?

00:41:17.780 --> 00:41:19.320
Iketani-san!

00:41:19.320 --> 00:41:21.950
I'm so glad to hear from you. Where are you now?

00:41:24.070 --> 00:41:26.790
Huh? You have a flat?

00:41:43.410 --> 00:41:46.100
I'm really sorry, Mako-chan.

00:41:46.560 --> 00:41:49.840
Not only was I late, I had to have you come get me...

00:41:50.990 --> 00:41:53.300
I'm really pathetic.

00:41:54.040 --> 00:41:56.900
No, please don't worry about it.

00:41:56.900 --> 00:41:58.410
We got to meet in the end.

00:42:00.020 --> 00:42:00.800
Yeah.

00:42:02.050 --> 00:42:03.600
Anyway,

00:42:03.600 --> 00:42:08.000
what was it that you wanted to tell me the other day, Iketani-san?

00:42:08.000 --> 00:42:08.770
Huh?

00:42:08.770 --> 00:42:10.220
That's...

00:42:10.220 --> 00:42:11.800
well...

00:42:11.800 --> 00:42:13.330
Crap.

00:42:13.330 --> 00:42:17.530
I've totally lost my momentum because of how pathetic this situation is.

00:42:21.690 --> 00:42:23.610
O-oh yeah,

00:42:23.610 --> 00:42:26.540
you said you had something to say too, Mako-chan.

00:42:26.540 --> 00:42:27.390
What was it about?

00:42:36.300 --> 00:42:37.760
So,

00:42:37.760 --> 00:42:39.490
I know it's rather sudden...

00:42:42.960 --> 00:42:45.080
but I'm moving to Tokyo.

00:42:45.080 --> 00:42:46.280
Huh?

00:42:46.280 --> 00:42:47.620
Tokyo?

00:42:59.820 --> 00:43:05.310
There was a promotion where a certain publishing company would sponsor an amateur to drive in races for a year...

00:43:05.310 --> 00:43:10.150
and that person's experiences would be published in a magazine.

00:43:10.150 --> 00:43:11.020
Okay.

00:43:11.630 --> 00:43:14.410
I applied for the heck of it,

00:43:15.160 --> 00:43:17.530
and for whatever reason...

00:43:17.530 --> 00:43:19.030
You got accepted?

00:43:21.360 --> 00:43:22.620
That's amazing!

00:43:22.620 --> 00:43:24.820
You're going to be a racer!

00:43:24.820 --> 00:43:30.570
Although it's just a race series sponsored by car makers with only minimal modifications allowed to vehicles...

00:43:30.570 --> 00:43:32.080
That's still amazing!

00:43:32.080 --> 00:43:33.140
Yeah,

00:43:33.140 --> 00:43:37.130
I hear that a huge sum of money is needed for someone to race for a full year.

00:43:38.040 --> 00:43:40.450
I couldn't possibly pay for it myself.

00:43:40.450 --> 00:43:41.530
I'm sure.

00:43:42.530 --> 00:43:45.010
I really wasn't sure,

00:43:45.010 --> 00:43:47.520
but I don't think a chance like this will come my way ever again.

00:43:51.020 --> 00:43:54.650
I just had to talk to you about this, Iketani-san.

00:43:55.570 --> 00:43:58.120
I think it's all thanks to you...

00:43:58.870 --> 00:44:01.200
that I've been able to keep driving this long, Iketani-san.

00:44:01.200 --> 00:44:04.100
W-what are you talking about, Mako-chan?

00:44:04.100 --> 00:44:05.580
That's not true at all.

00:44:05.580 --> 00:44:08.510
No, I don't think I would've had this opportunity

00:44:09.500 --> 00:44:13.960
if I hadn't met you, Iketani-san.

00:44:13.960 --> 00:44:16.500
Oh man...

00:44:18.720 --> 00:44:20.920
Either way, I'm glad to hear that.

00:44:20.920 --> 00:44:22.680
Congratulations, Mako-chan.

00:44:26.110 --> 00:44:30.460
I can't believe that someone I know is going to become a racer!

00:44:30.460 --> 00:44:34.940
I'll brag about you to all my friends when you become famous!

00:44:34.940 --> 00:44:37.150
When you do, please give me your first autograph.

00:44:37.150 --> 00:44:40.490
Oh no, what are you talking about?

00:44:40.490 --> 00:44:42.040
No, I'm serious.

00:44:42.040 --> 00:44:43.080
I'm impressed.

00:44:43.080 --> 00:44:44.360
You're great, Mako-chan!

00:44:48.190 --> 00:44:50.650
She's actually happy about it.

00:44:50.650 --> 00:44:52.640
Well yeah,

00:44:52.640 --> 00:44:54.020
why wouldn't she be.

00:44:54.870 --> 00:44:58.400
Oh, I've been doing all the talking,

00:44:58.400 --> 00:45:00.380
but I want to hear what you have to say too, Iketani-san.

00:45:00.380 --> 00:45:02.090
W-well,

00:45:02.090 --> 00:45:03.880
what I had to say was...

00:45:04.750 --> 00:45:06.350
This isn't good.

00:45:06.350 --> 00:45:09.390
Compared to what you just told me, it's nothing at all.

00:45:09.390 --> 00:45:12.270
That's not true, please tell me!

00:45:12.270 --> 00:45:15.840
No, it really was nothing.

00:45:15.840 --> 00:45:19.730
See, I wanted to properly apologize for what happened last year.

00:45:19.730 --> 00:45:22.970
And it looks like I have your understanding already.

00:45:22.970 --> 00:45:24.910
So it's all right.

00:45:26.050 --> 00:45:27.530
Is that so?

00:45:27.530 --> 00:45:28.580
Yeah.

00:45:41.500 --> 00:45:45.030
I actually want to tell her, "Don't go."

00:45:45.030 --> 00:45:45.950
But...

00:45:46.930 --> 00:45:49.700
But... I can't do it.

00:45:52.330 --> 00:45:53.560
Iketani-san...

00:45:54.540 --> 00:45:56.060
Mako-chan...

00:45:56.470 --> 00:46:02.370
Well, I need to call a tow truck to fix up my car and drive it home.

00:46:02.370 --> 00:46:06.200
I'm sorry, but do you think you can drop me off somewhere near a phone?

00:46:12.160 --> 00:46:13.200
Okay?

00:46:33.780 --> 00:46:35.100
What?!

00:46:35.100 --> 00:46:39.140
So you came back without confessing your feelings?

00:46:39.140 --> 00:46:40.820
I mean,

00:46:40.820 --> 00:46:43.070
how could I say it under those circumstances?

00:46:43.070 --> 00:46:47.570
You might say that, but your feelings will never reach her if you don't tell her!

00:46:47.570 --> 00:46:49.390
It's okay.

00:46:51.450 --> 00:46:59.990
Since Mako-chan's leaving for Tokyo to start racing, confessing my feelings will only trouble her.

00:46:59.990 --> 00:47:01.330
But man...

00:47:01.330 --> 00:47:04.120
It might make me feel good,

00:47:04.120 --> 00:47:06.550
but that's only self-satisfaction.

00:47:06.550 --> 00:47:10.050
This was the right choice when you think about the other person's feelings.

00:47:16.100 --> 00:47:22.370
Telling her, "Give it your best," and cheering her on is the best I can do.

00:47:23.460 --> 00:47:26.400
You're too nice...

00:47:27.650 --> 00:47:28.570
Maybe.

00:47:33.700 --> 00:47:36.850
That's pretty cold of Iketani.

00:47:37.680 --> 00:47:41.220
I thought he had feelings for you too.

00:47:41.220 --> 00:47:43.790
I really don't get men.

00:47:43.790 --> 00:47:45.730
It's okay, Sayuki.

00:47:45.730 --> 00:47:48.010
Now I can move on.

00:47:48.010 --> 00:47:49.240
Really?

00:47:49.900 --> 00:47:52.650
To be honest, I was worried.

00:47:52.650 --> 00:47:55.580
Life in Tokyo seems tough.

00:47:55.580 --> 00:48:01.210
I wasn't confident that a wimp like me could become a racer.

00:48:01.830 --> 00:48:03.960
I was hesitant until the last minute,

00:48:03.960 --> 00:48:09.160
so much so that I could've been swayed had someone told me not to go.

00:48:11.860 --> 00:48:14.600
But now I'm embarrassed that I even thought that.

00:48:14.600 --> 00:48:19.130
I'm sure Iketani-san was cold to me because he saw through all that.

00:48:21.710 --> 00:48:24.970
He gave me a push on the back saying,

00:48:24.970 --> 00:48:27.740
"Go give it a try with confidence,"

00:48:27.740 --> 00:48:29.750
so that I won't leave any unnecessary regrets over here.

00:48:30.570 --> 00:48:32.110
That's what I'd like to think.

00:48:35.180 --> 00:48:36.860
That might be true.

00:48:36.860 --> 00:48:38.970
He does have an admirable side to him like that.

00:48:38.970 --> 00:48:42.080
I get a feeling that's true.

00:48:46.490 --> 00:48:47.780
Iketani,

00:48:47.780 --> 00:48:49.400
do you really...

00:48:49.780 --> 00:48:52.530
have no regrets?

00:48:53.690 --> 00:48:55.020
Nope.

00:48:55.020 --> 00:48:56.380
It's tough,

00:48:56.380 --> 00:48:57.490
but I have no regrets.

00:48:58.430 --> 00:49:01.330
This is how it was supposed to be.

00:49:10.620 --> 00:49:11.630
Mako...

00:49:19.510 --> 00:49:21.600
Good luck!

00:49:21.600 --> 00:49:24.890
I certify your talents.

00:49:24.890 --> 00:49:25.960
Yeah,

00:49:25.960 --> 00:49:27.850
I'll go as far as I can.

00:49:28.570 --> 00:49:30.040
I won't hesitate anymore.

00:49:31.390 --> 00:49:34.620
So this is the end for Impact Blue.

00:49:34.620 --> 00:49:36.820
It's a little sad.

00:49:53.840 --> 00:49:56.200
I need to practice more.

00:49:56.200 --> 00:50:00.100
I blew my tire at a time like that because my skills are still lacking.

00:50:02.890 --> 00:50:05.850
Will you go practice with me, Kenji?

00:50:05.860 --> 00:50:06.800
Yeah.

00:50:26.410 --> 00:50:28.420
Takumi told me this before,

00:50:28.420 --> 00:50:32.430
but I guess I push it too far when I get pumped up.

00:50:34.340 --> 00:50:35.840
Next up is the S-curve.

00:50:35.840 --> 00:50:37.050
All right!

00:50:45.100 --> 00:50:47.620
This is the last run for Impact Blue.

00:50:48.360 --> 00:50:50.480
Please take a good look, Sayuki.

00:50:50.480 --> 00:50:51.410
Yeah,

00:50:51.410 --> 00:50:53.110
give me a refreshing run,

00:50:53.110 --> 00:50:55.640
Impact Blue's shooting star.

00:51:09.710 --> 00:51:12.990
You still have some work to do. You're ballooning out too far to the outside.

00:51:12.990 --> 00:51:13.650
Okay.

00:51:14.710 --> 00:51:17.110
But this is great.

00:51:17.830 --> 00:51:20.860
When I'm driving like this, I can forget everything.

00:51:21.360 --> 00:51:23.510
I might not be as fast as Takumi,

00:51:23.510 --> 00:51:25.420
but I must be a racer at heart too.

00:54:29.880 --> 00:54:32.760
Street racers...

00:54:32.760 --> 00:54:36.290
don't need girlfriends!
